  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Playing through the lines",
  "description": "Played on a 9v9 pitch split into thirds. Cones or poles are spread out in each third and act as opponents. One team in its formation – the diagram shows 3-3-2 – plays the ball from its own goalkeeper to the goalkeeper at the other end (J) and must go through all three thirds. Offside applies. When the ball arrives, the team starts again with a new ball from the same goalkeeper. With two teams, they can play at the same time in opposite directions, each with its own ball.\n\nVary how the ball is played to the goalkeeper. Play two minutes at a time with a minute of mobility in between.\n\nProgression: replace the cones with defenders, two in each third, who defend their zone. If they win the ball they counter, and the team that lost it tries to win it back. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Stand between the opponents (cones), not behind them – then you can receive and turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Width and depth in every unit so there are always at least two passing lanes."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Check over your shoulder before the ball arrives so you know if you can turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "A firm pass along the ground past a unit beats a safe pass sideways."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 3,
